The lake, drawn over the areas it cuts into. Not something the reader switches on:
every map of Zurich in the corpus has it, and one without it reads as a mistake.
Implied by the geography, because not every geography has a lake to draw - the
Swiss cantons have none, and the statistical zones include the lake as areas of
their own.

// #hidden
// #label Lake
// #hint The lake, drawn over the map.

// #region mapDataTypes
lakeFeatures: import("d3").GeoPermissibleObjects;
// #endregion

// #region mapData
lakeFeatures: topojson.feature(topo, topo.objects[__LAKE_LAYER__]),
// #endregion

// #region mapProps
.lakeFeatures(state.mapData.lakeFeatures)
// #endregion
